700001-e6329c7f-1b8f-4b2b-b84d-47f7a41b9a73"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"938317f399c879743163bdcd0fbe81a7d61baf90dfcf9eb0d599364eb497861d","event_uuid":"be388f98-243d-4119-bb7a-d47ed261ca15","position":{"commit_sha":"3cfa10b7207c359235d38135857264ee2ad97be2","position":"1788830865794339001-be388f98-243d-4119-bb7a-d47ed261ca15"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"60c324ee01be39b81ea131f2b0e35bf973d200f7b99e216e871e4fdc982d38e0","event_uuid":"ad5f3903-8d99-4558-b3d6-d63c16015bb2","position":{"commit_sha":"4f3cdf85cebda2d939aed5052e58937f6f7f45e4","position":"1788830889842537001-ad5f3903-8d99-4558-b3d6-d63c16015bb2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: alarm work APPROVED — mirror existing alarm best practices in this environment; every alarm must provide meaningful health signal, not noise.","timestamp":1788816823278154001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lead 1 settled before code change: 8h CloudWatch sweep after 2684/5993 deploy showed head metrics gerrit_healthy, reviewbot_healthy, GerritReachable, mcp_healthy, root_disk_used_percent, gate_scratch_mounted, plus probe_ok/probe_elapsed_seconds/probe_truncated all at 85 datapoints with 10.0 minute max inter-arrival; the prior 25 minute head gap narrowed after 2684. Remaining independent publishing defect implemented/tested in worktree alm-a7bd: main probe now falls back to cached region and instance id when IMDS misses, matching the stop hook's cache pattern so successful head health probes do not publish with empty --region/InstanceId.","timestamp":1788817450658079001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completed in Gerrit change 2802, patch set 2, submitted as 59850948619e66c5cd3b5d44ca293eda573981d0. Measurement: post-2684 8h CloudWatch sweep showed 85 datapoints and 10.0 minute max inter-arrival for head metrics and probe liveness metrics, so lead 1 narrowed the earlier 25 minute gap. Fix: main observability probe now reuses cached region/instance-id when IMDS misses, refreshes both caches on good reads, and logs head put-metric-data failures to journald instead of swallowing them. Validation: RED regression test for cached metadata/put failure, cache refresh test, full timeout-observability test module, make lint, and full make verify passed. No Terraform apply required; no alarms created or modified.","timestamp":1788830179491700001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788642362155989053,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"88b152df-0c36-497d-a773-dd83b92bdfd0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9313-1fac-9f32-4b07"},{"link_uuid":"ea7169e9-977d-4b12-ae5c-07e47b10406d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7d64-4b7c-3574-4f06"},{"link_uuid":"bb435219-4b0e-47b5-a676-c84453f5bc69","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f075-2955-c0ee-4d49"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`rebar/host` metrics published from the FIRST ~200 lines of `infra/scripts/observability.sh` —\n`gerrit_healthy`, `reviewbot_healthy`, `GerritReachable`, `mcp_healthy`, `disk_used_percent`,\n`root_disk_used_percent`, `gate_scratch_mounted` — show a max gap of **25 minutes**, widening\nfrom 10 minutes in an earlier sweep the same day. At 20:47Z on 2026-09-05 that produced **four\nsimultaneous false alarms** (root-disk-pressure, gerrit-data-disk-high, gerrit-gate-down,\nmcp-serving-path-down), every StateReason naming \"missing datapoints were treated as\nBreaching\", while the underlying conditions were verified healthy: Gerrit HTTP 200 in 0.27 s,\nroot disk 71-76% against an 85% threshold, `disk_used_percent` = 20.\n\n## Why this is NOT bug 9313 (ignitable-fuchsia-kawala)\n\n`9313` is the section-truncation defect: the probe is SIGTERM-ed on its 240s `TimeoutStartSec`\ninside the docker `du`, so every metric published AFTER that point vanishes. It is proven in\nsitu, and change 2684 fixes it.\n\n**It cannot produce a head gap.** The head runs BEFORE the docker walk. The breadcrumb trace\ntaken for `9313` covers ten consecutive killed runs and shows, in every one of them, the\nprologue completing in **7-13 seconds** and the gate-scratch breadcrumb (line 214, the last\nhead section) landing normally — then 231 seconds of silence, then the kill. The head sections\nrun to completion on runs that are killed.\n\nA 25-minute head gap is roughly **four to five missed runs** at the observed 5-6 minute\ncadence. Whatever causes it either drops whole runs or fails the head's\n`aws cloudwatch put-metric-data` calls. Both are outside `9313`'s mechanism.\n\nThis ticket exists so that the head gap is investigated on its own evidence rather than folded\ninto `9313` on a plausible story — the exact error `9313`'s own investigation had to correct\ntwice.\n\n## Leads, explicitly UNCONFIRMED\n\n1. **Cadence pressure.** A killed run occupies 240s of a ~300s timer period, leaving ~60s of\n   slack, so any additional delay pushes a run past the next elapse. Change 2684 takes a run to\n   ~105s, restoring ~195s. **If the head gap narrows after 2684 deploys, this was a\n   contributing factor.** If it does not, the defect is independent. Check this FIRST — it is\n   free, and it partitions the search.\n2. **The `aws` CLI itself.** It is a Python process started fresh for every metric; under the\n   memory pressure documented on this host (the mcp container at ~1.7 GB RSS) its startup could\n   be slow or it could be killed. A failing `put-metric-data` is invisible today: every call is\n   `2>/dev/null || true`.\n3. **Timer elapse being skipped.** `OnUnitActiveSec` is measured from the last COMPLETED\n   activation; `1205-63b2-2c01-4e7f` already found one latch mode here.\n\n## What makes this diagnosable now\n\nChange 2684 publishes `probe_ok`, `probe_elapsed_seconds` and `probe_truncated`. Before it,\nrun duration and run completion were visible only in `systemctl` and in no metric at all —\nwhich is why `9313` took a day. Start this investigation from those three, not from the\nabsence of other metrics.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The head gap is reproduced and attributed by measurement — whether a run was started, and\n      whether the head's `put-metric-data` calls succeeded — not inferred from metric absence.\n- [x] Lead 1 is settled first: state whether the gap narrows after 2684 deploys, with numbers.\n- [x] If the `aws` calls are failing, their failure becomes observable rather than swallowed by\n      `2>/dev/null || true`.\n- [x] The four alarms named above stop firing on absence while their conditions are healthy,\n      without their thresholds changing.\n- [x] Portability: host shell + systemd + local validation; no dependence on a single CI provider.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound 2026-09-05 by an independent CloudWatch presence sweep (period=300, 96 buckets/metric)\nrun while `9313` was in review. The sweep's headline finding — a monotone decline in metric\npresence with script position, 93% at the head down to 43% at the tail and 0% for\n`var_tmp_used_percent` — CONFIRMS `9313`. The head number is the residue that `9313` does not\nexplain, and this ticket is that residue.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Cache and reuse valid EC2 metadata so head-of-script CloudWatch publishes do not use empty region/instance id when IMDS misses."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_timeout_9313.py","reason":"Regression test for the head metrics publishing path when IMDS fails but cached metadata exists."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7d64-4b7c-3574-4f06"],["relates_to","f075-2955-c0ee-4d49"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"be388f98-243d-4119-bb7a-d47ed261ca15","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a7bd-0cee-404f-4c06","ticket_type":"bug","title":"The observability probe's HEAD-of-script metrics gap for up to 25 minutes, which the section-truncation root cause cannot explain — a second, independent publishing defect","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5bc01e2d-18cb-45fd-ae3c-5e4c13c32667","30af5159-db63-46e0-8f69-77138e943cdc","97ad2acb-092a-4212-b042-4379ab1b3e25","7f9d6875-76bf-411e-9c77-3ab50b9bb896","ece36402-9047-48a4-8ebc-4d15241e2332","c6e89bd5-536a-420b-b092-a3b1b9192cea","ea7169e9-977d-4b12-ae5c-07e47b10406d","bb435219-4b0e-47b5-a676-c84453f5bc69","17d53250-5a3a-489a-b418-9bf95a3941af","e6329c7f-1b8f-4b2b-b84d-47f7a41b9a73","be388f98-243d-4119-bb7a-d47ed261ca15","ad5f3903-8d99-4558-b3d6-d63c16015bb2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788848498502579836,"uuid":"3172fb91-9679-423e-a949-3409ddcc5656"}